    section: "I", questionRef: "2021 HL Section I Q(a)",
    questionText: "Profile the way that two Pre-Christian rituals have been adapted by a Christian tradition in Ireland today.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal"}, totalMarks: 80,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Samhain, the Pre-Christian festival where the dead were said to roam the land of the living, has been adapted by Christians today with both the Roman Catholic and Anglican traditions honouring those who have died in the feast of All Saints and All Souls etc.", marks: null, contextNote: "An excellent answer will show an understanding of how the Christian message was inculturated in the Irish context by accurately tracing how two Pre-Christian rituals have been adapted into the Christian tradition in Ireland today e.g.", openList: true },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "St Brigid’s day on the 1st of February was adapted from the Pre-Christian festival of Imbolc, which marked the beginning of Spring and the fertility of the land; Christianity adopted 1st of February to honour Saint Brigid of Kildare etc.", marks: null, openList: true },
    ],
